        "original_id": "c98d6a48-28ea-5aa3-9c92-a1f2ac230ca8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Captain Horatio Hornblower, To Kill a Mockingbird\n- People: Gregory Peck, Virginia Mayo, Robert Beatty, Terence Morgan, Gerry Mitchell, Raoul Walsh\n- Organizations: Warner Bros., Royal Navy, Academy Awards\n- Topics: film credits, acting awards\n\nFacts:\n- Captain Horatio Hornblower, also known in the UK as Captain Horatio Hornblower R.N., is a 1951 American naval swashbuckling war film in Technicolor from Warner Bros.\n- In the title Captain Horatio Hornblower R.N., the abbreviation R.N. stands for Royal Navy.\n- Gerry Mitchell produced Captain Horatio Hornblower, and Raoul Walsh directed it.\n- Gregory Peck, Virginia Mayo, Robert Beatty, and Terence Morgan starred in Captain Horatio Hornblower.\n- Gregory Peck won the Academy Award for Best Actor for his performance as Atticus Finch in the 1962 film To Kill a Mockingbird.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
